by nicolas-grekas at 2026-10-14T16:29:15Z

Thanks @lazerg. I squashed a fix into your commit. The escaping now runs after `setColumnMaxWidth()` wraps the cell. Before, `abcd|efgh` at width 5 gave `abcd\` on one row and `|efgh` on the next one. Wrapped lines now become `<br>` too, so a markdown cell never spans several rows.

I kept your backslash case, but the backslash is now doubled. With `Line 1\<br>`, markdown reads `\<` as an escaped `<` and shows `<br>` as text. A lone `\r` also becomes `<br>` now.
